return [
    // Overview
    'JWT attacks' => 'Serangan JWT',
    "In this section, we'll look at how design issues and flawed handling of JSON web tokens (JWTs) can leave websites vulnerable to a variety of high-severity attacks. As JWTs are most commonly used in authentication, session management, and access control mechanisms, these vulnerabilities can potentially compromise the entire website and its users." => 'Pada bagian ini, kami membahas bagaimana cacat desain dan penanganan JSON Web Token (JWT) membuka celah berisiko tinggi pada autentikasi, sesi, dan kontrol akses.',
    "Don't worry if you're not familiar with JWTs and how they work - we'll cover all of the relevant details as we go. We've also provided a number of deliberately vulnerable labs so that you can practice exploiting these vulnerabilities safely against realistic targets." => 'Seluruh struktur dasar JWT dijelaskan beriringan dengan lab praktik yang sengaja dibuat rentan.',
    "If you're already familiar with the basic concepts behind JWT attacks and just want to practice exploiting them on some realistic, deliberately vulnerable targets, you can access all of the labs in this topic from the link below." => 'Jika Anda sudah memahami konsep dasar serangan JWT dan ingin berlatih eksploitasi pada target realistis, akses semua lab topik ini lewat tautan di bawah.',
    'View all JWT labs' => 'Lihat semua lab JWT',
    'From [[A0]]Burp Suite Professional 2022.5.1[[/A0]], Burp Scanner can automatically detect a number of vulnerabilities in JWT mechanisms on your behalf. For more information, see the related issue definitions on the <strong>Target &gt; Issued definitions</strong> tab.' => 'Berbagai celah JWT ini juga dapat diuji otomatis menggunakan pemindai kerentanan maupun secara manual di [[A0]]semua lab JWT[[/A0]].',
    'What are JWTs?' => 'Apa itu JWT?',
    'JSON web tokens (JWTs) are a standardized format for sending cryptographically signed JSON data between systems. They can theoretically contain any kind of data, but are most commonly used to send information ("claims") about users as part of authentication, session handling, and access control mechanisms.' => 'JSON Web Token (JWT) adalah format standar untuk mengirim data JSON bertanda tangan kriptografis, umumnya membawa klaim identitas dan hak akses pengguna.',
    'Unlike with classic session tokens, all of the data that a server needs is stored client-side within the JWT itself. This makes JWTs a popular choice for highly distributed websites where users need to interact seamlessly with multiple back-end servers.' => 'Berbeda dengan token sesi tradisional, seluruh klaim tersimpan langsung di sisi klien di dalam token sehingga cocok untuk arsitektur terdistribusi.',
    'JWT format' => 'Format JWT',
    'A JWT consists of 3 parts: a [[S0]]header[[/S0]], a [[S1]]payload[[/S1]], and a [[S2]]signature[[/S2]]. These are each separated by a dot, as shown in the following example:' => 'JWT terdiri atas 3 bagian yang dipisah tanda titik: [[S0]]header[[/S0]], [[S1]]payload[[/S1]], dan [[S2]]tanda tangan[[/S2]], seperti contoh berikut:',
    'The header and payload parts of a JWT are just base64url-encoded JSON objects. The header contains metadata about the token itself, while the payload contains the actual "claims" about the user. For example, you can decode the payload from the token above to reveal the following claims:' => 'Header dan payload hanyalah objek JSON yang di-encode Base64URL. Jika payload di atas didekode, isinya terbaca jelas:',
    'In most cases, this data can be easily read or modified by anyone with access to the token. Therefore, the security of any JWT-based mechanism is heavily reliant on the cryptographic signature.' => 'Karena isi token mudah dibaca dan diubah siapa saja, keamanan JWT bergantung penuh pada verifikasi tanda tangan kriptografis.',
    'JWT signature' => 'Tanda tangan JWT',
    'The server that issues the token typically generates the signature by hashing the header and payload. In some cases, they also encrypt the resulting hash. Either way, this process involves a secret signing key. This mechanism provides a way for servers to verify that none of the data within the token has been tampered with since it was issued:' => 'Server penerbit membuat tanda tangan atas gabungan header dan payload memakai kunci rahasia guna memastikan integritas token:',
    'As the signature is directly derived from the rest of the token, changing a single byte of the header or payload results in a mismatched signature.' => 'Mengubah satu byte saja di header atau payload langsung membuat tanda tangan tidak cocok.',
    "Without knowing the server's secret signing key, it shouldn't be possible to generate the correct signature for a given header or payload." => 'Tanpa mengetahui kunci rahasia server, penyerang semestinya tak bisa menghasilkan tanda tangan yang sah.',
    'If you want to gain a better understanding of how JWTs are constructed, you can use the debugger on [[C0]] to experiment with arbitrary tokens.' => 'Anda bisa bereksperimen mendekode maupun merangkai struktur JWT lewat debugger [[C0]].',
    'JWT vs JWS vs JWE' => 'JWT vs JWS vs JWE',
    'The JWT specification is actually very limited. It only defines a format for representing information ("claims") as a JSON object that can be transferred between two parties. In practice, JWTs aren\'t really used as a standalone entity. The JWT spec is extended by both the JSON Web Signature (JWS) and JSON Web Encryption (JWE) specifications, which define concrete ways of actually implementing JWTs.' => 'Spesifikasi inti JWT hanya mendefinisikan format klaim JSON, lalu diperluas oleh JWS (untuk tanda tangan) dan JWE (untuk enkripsi isi).',
    'In other words, a JWT is usually either a JWS or JWE token. When people use the term "JWT", they almost always mean a JWS token. JWEs are very similar, except that the actual contents of the token are encrypted rather than just encoded.' => 'Di lapangan, sebutan "JWT" hampir selalu merujuk ke token JWS karena isinya hanya di-encode, bukan dienkripsi seperti JWE.',
    'For simplicity, throughout these materials, "JWT" refers primarily to JWS tokens, although some of the vulnerabilities described may also apply to JWE tokens.' => 'Untuk menyederhanakan pembahasan, istilah JWT di sini merujuk terutama pada token JWS.',
    'What are JWT attacks?' => 'Apa itu serangan JWT?',
    'JWT attacks involve a user sending modified JWTs to the server in order to achieve a malicious goal. Typically, this goal is to bypass authentication and access controls by impersonating another user who has already been authenticated.' => 'Serangan JWT dilakukan dengan memodifikasi isi atau header JWT guna meniru identitas pengguna lain atau menaikkan hak akses.',
    'What is the impact of JWT attacks?' => 'Apa dampak serangan JWT?',
    'The impact of JWT attacks is usually severe. If an attacker is able to create their own valid tokens with arbitrary values, they may be able to escalate their own privileges or impersonate other users, taking full control of their accounts.' => 'Dampaknya umumnya kritis karena penyerang yang mampu memalsukan token dapat mengambil alih akun mana pun atau menjadi admin.',
    'How do vulnerabilities to JWT attacks arise?' => 'Bagaimana celah serangan JWT muncul?',
    'JWT vulnerabilities typically arise due to flawed JWT handling within the application itself. The [[A0]]various specifications[[/A0]] related to JWTs are relatively flexible by design, allowing website developers to decide many implementation details for themselves. This can result in them accidentally introducing vulnerabilities even when using battle-hardened libraries.' => 'Kerentanan muncul dari cara aplikasi mengonfigurasi verifikasi token pada pustaka JWT yang sering terlalu fleksibel mengikuti [[A0]]beragam spesifikasi[[/A0]].',
    "These implementation flaws usually mean that the signature of the JWT is not verified properly. This enables an attacker to tamper with the values passed to the application via the token's payload. Even if the signature is robustly verified, whether it can truly be trusted relies heavily on the server's secret key remaining a secret. If this key is leaked in some way, or can be guessed or brute-forced, an attacker can generate a valid signature for any arbitrary token, compromising the entire mechanism." => 'Celah timbul jika tanda tangan tidak diperiksa dengan benar, atau jika kunci rahasia penandatanganan lemah sehingga mudah di-brute-force.',
    'How to work with JWTs in Burp Suite' => 'Cara menguji JWT',
    'In case you haven\'t worked with JWTs in the past, we recommend familiarizing yourself with the relevant features of Burp Suite before attempting the labs in this topic.' => 'Pahami cara membaca, mengubah payload Base64URL, dan menandatangani ulang JWT sebelum masuk ke lab.',
    'Working with JWTs in Burp Suite' => 'Bekerja dengan JWT di lab praktik',
    'Exploiting flawed JWT signature verification' => 'Mengeksploitasi verifikasi tanda tangan JWT yang cacat',
    'By design, servers don\'t usually store any information about the JWTs that they issue. Instead, each token is an entirely self-contained entity. This has several advantages, but also introduces a fundamental problem - the server doesn\'t actually know anything about the original contents of the token, or even what the original signature was. Therefore, if the server doesn\'t verify the signature properly, there\'s nothing to stop an attacker from making arbitrary changes to the rest of the token.' => 'Karena bersifat stateless, server tidak menyimpan salinan isi JWT asli dan hanya bergantung pada verifikasi tanda tangan.',
    'For example, consider a JWT containing the following claims:' => 'Perhatikan contoh klaim JWT berikut:',
    'If the server identifies the session based on this [[C0]], modifying its value might enable an attacker to impersonate other logged-in users. Similarly, if the [[C1]] value is used for access control, this could provide a simple vector for privilege escalation.' => 'Mengubah nilai [[C0]] atau [[C1]] tanpa ditolak verifikasi tanda tangan langsung memberi akses ke akun lain atau hak admin.',
    'In the first couple of labs, you\'ll see some examples of how these vulnerabilities might look in real-world applications.' => 'Dua lab pertama memperlihatkan bentuk celah verifikasi yang paling umum.',
    'Accepting arbitrary signatures' => 'Menerima tanda tangan sembarang',
    'JWT libraries typically provide one method for verifying tokens and another that just decodes them. For example, the Node.js library [[C0]] has [[C1]] and [[C2]].' => 'Pustaka JWT seperti [[C0]] biasanya menyediakan fungsi [[C1]] (memeriksa tanda tangan) dan [[C2]] (sekadar membaca payload).',
    'Occasionally, developers confuse these two methods and only pass incoming tokens to the [[C0]] method. This effectively means that the application doesn\'t verify the signature at all.' => 'Jika pengembang keliru memanggil [[C0]] saja, aplikasi sama sekali tidak memverifikasi tanda tangan token.',
    'Accepting tokens with no signature' => 'Menerima token tanpa tanda tangan',
    'Among other things, the JWT header contains an [[C0]] parameter. This tells the server which algorithm was used to sign the token and, therefore, which algorithm it needs to use when verifying the signature.' => 'Header JWT mencantumkan parameter [[C0]] yang memberi tahu server algoritma apa yang dipakai untuk memverifikasi token:',
    'This is inherently flawed because the server has no option but to implicitly trust user-controllable input from the token which, at this point, hasn\'t been verified at all. In other words, an attacker can directly influence how the server checks whether the token is trustworthy.' => 'Mengandalkan input mentah dari token klien berarti penyerang ikut menentukan cara server memverifikasi token yang belum tepercaya.',
    'JWTs can be signed using a range of different algorithms, but can also be left unsigned. In this case, the [[C0]] parameter is set to [[C1]], which indicates a so-called "unsecured JWT". Due to the obvious dangers of this, servers usually reject tokens with no signature. However, as this kind of filtering relies on string parsing, you can sometimes bypass these filters using classic obfuscation techniques, such as mixed capitalization and unexpected encodings.' => 'Nilai [[C0]] berupa [[C1]] menandakan token tanpa tanda tangan. Filter string yang hanya menolak nilai persis kadang lolos memakai variasi kapitalisasi atau karakter kontrol.',
    'Even if the token is unsigned, the payload part must still be terminated with a trailing dot.' => 'Token tanpa tanda tangan tetap wajib mempertahankan tanda titik penutup setelah bagian payload.',
    'Brute-forcing secret keys' => 'Brute-force kunci rahasia JWT',
    'Some signing algorithms, such as HS256 (HMAC + SHA-256), use an arbitrary, standalone string as the secret key. Just like a password, it\'s crucial that this secret can\'t be easily guessed or brute-forced by an attacker. Otherwise, they may be able to create JWTs with any header and payload values they like, then use the key to re-sign the token with a valid signature.' => 'Algoritma simetris seperti HS256 memakai kunci rahasia berupa string yang jika lemah bisa di-brute-force untuk memalsukan tanda tangan sah.',
    'When implementing JWT applications, developers sometimes make mistakes like forgetting to change default or placeholder secrets. They may even copy and paste code snippets they find online, then forget to change a hardcoded secret that\'s provided as an example. In this case, it can be trivial for an attacker to brute-force a server\'s secret using a [[A0]]wordlist of well-known secrets[[/A0]].' => 'Kunci bawaan atau contoh kode yang lupa diganti mudah dipecahkan memakai [[A0]]daftar rahasia JWT umum[[/A0]].',
    'Brute-forcing secret keys using hashcat' => 'Brute-force kunci rahasia memakai hashcat',
    'We recommend using hashcat to brute-force secret keys. You can [[A0]]install hashcat manually[[/A0]], but it also comes pre-installed and ready to use on Kali Linux.' => 'Alat seperti hashcat dapat melakukan brute-force secara luring dan sangat cepat ([[A0]]panduan instalasi[[/A0]]).',
    'If you\'re using the pre-built VirtualBox image for Kali rather than the bare metal installer version, this may not have enough memory allocated to run hashcat.' => 'Pastikan mesin memiliki alokasi memori memadai saat menjalankan hashcat.',
    'You just need a valid, signed JWT from the target server and a [[A0]]wordlist of well-known secrets[[/A0]]. You can then run the following command, passing in the JWT and wordlist as arguments:' => 'Berbekal satu JWT valid dan [[A0]]daftar rahasia umum[[/A0]], jalankan perintah berikut:',
    'Hashcat signs the header and payload from the JWT using each secret in the wordlist, then compares the resulting signature with the original one from the server. If any of the signatures match, hashcat outputs the identified secret in the following format, along with various other details:' => 'Jika ada kandidat kunci yang menghasilkan tanda tangan identik, rahasia tersebut akan dicetak dengan format:',
    'If you run the command more than once, you need to include the [[C0]] flag to output the results.' => 'Untuk menjalankan ulang tanpa menghitung ulang, tambahkan flag [[C0]].',
    "As hashcat runs locally on your machine and doesn't rely on sending requests to the server, this process is extremely quick, even when using a huge wordlist." => 'Karena dijalankan lokal tanpa mengirim lalu lintas ke server target, pemecahan berlangsung sangat cepat.',
    'Once you have identified the secret key, you can use it to generate a valid signature for any JWT header and payload that you like. For details on how to re-sign a modified JWT in Burp Suite, see [[A0]]Editing JWTs[[/A0]].' => 'Begitu kunci rahasia ditemukan, Anda dapat menandatangani ulang JWT dengan klaim sembarang.',
    'If the server uses an extremely weak secret, it may even be possible to brute-force this character-by-character rather than using a wordlist.' => 'Untuk rahasia sangat pendek, serangan brute-force berbasis mask karakter juga dimungkinkan.',
    'JWT header parameter injections' => 'Injeksi parameter header JWT',
    'According to the JWS specification, only the [[C0]] header parameter is mandatory. In practice, however, JWT headers (also known as JOSE headers) often contain several other parameters. The following ones are of particular interest to attackers.' => 'Selain [[C0]] yang wajib ada, header JOSE JWT sering memuat parameter opsional yang berisiko:',
    '[[C0]] (JSON Web Key) - Provides an embedded JSON object representing the key.' => '[[C0]] (JSON Web Key): menyematkan objek kunci JSON langsung di dalam header token.',
    '[[C0]] (JSON Web Key Set URL) - Provides a URL from which servers can fetch a set of keys containing the correct key.' => '[[C0]] (JWK Set URL): menunjuk ke URL tempat server mengambil kumpulan kunci verifikasi.',
    '[[C0]] (Key ID) - Provides an ID that servers can use to identify the correct key in cases where there are multiple keys to choose from. Depending on the format of the key, this may have a matching [[C1]] parameter.' => '[[C0]] (Key ID): pengenal kunci saat server memakai banyak kunci, kadang dipadankan dengan [[C1]] di JWK.',
    'As you can see, these user-controllable parameters each tell the recipient server which key to use when verifying the signature. In this section, you\'ll learn how to exploit these to inject modified JWTs signed using your own arbitrary key rather than the server\'s secret.' => 'Semua parameter header tersebut dapat disetel penyerang untuk mengarahkan server memverifikasi token memakai kunci buatan penyerang sendiri.',
    'Injecting self-signed JWTs via the jwk parameter' => 'Menyuntikkan JWT bertanda tangan sendiri melalui parameter jwk',
    'The JSON Web Signature (JWS) specification describes an optional [[C0]] header parameter, which servers can use to embed their public key directly within the token itself in JWK format.' => 'Parameter opsional [[C0]] memungkinkan kunci publik disematkan langsung di dalam header JWT dalam format JWK.',
    'JWK' => 'JWK',
    'A JWK (JSON Web Key) is a standardized format for representing keys as a JSON object.' => 'JWK (JSON Web Key) adalah format standar JSON untuk merepresentasikan kunci kriptografi.',
    'You can see an example of this in the following JWT header:' => 'Contoh header JWT yang memuat parameter jwk:',
    'Public and private keys' => 'Kunci publik dan kunci privat',
    'In case you\'re not familiar with the terms "public key" and "private key", we\'ve covered this as part of our materials on algorithm confusion attacks. For more information, see [[A0]]Symmetric vs asymmetric algorithms[[/A0]].' => 'Penjelasan mengenai pasangan kunci publik dan privat tersedia di halaman [[A0]]Algoritma simetris vs asimetris[[/A0]].',
    'Ideally, servers should only use a limited whitelist of public keys to verify JWT signatures. However, misconfigured servers sometimes use any key that\'s embedded in the [[C0]] parameter.' => 'Server yang salah konfigurasi terkadang langsung memakai kunci apa pun yang disematkan pada parameter [[C0]] tanpa memeriksa whitelist.',
    'You can exploit this behavior by signing a modified JWT using your own RSA private key, then embedding the matching public key in the [[C0]] header.' => 'Penyerang cukup menandatangani token pakai kunci privat RSA miliknya lalu menaruh kunci publik pasangannya di header [[C0]].',
    'Although you can manually add or modify the [[C0]] parameter in Burp, the [[A0]]JWT Editor extension[[/A0]] provides a useful feature to help you test for this vulnerability:' => 'Langkah membuat pasangan kunci RSA baru dan menyematkan [[C0]] dapat diringkas seperti berikut (atau otomatis dengan [[A0]]ekstensi JWT Editor[[/A0]]):',
    'With the extension loaded, in Burp\'s main tab bar, go to the <strong>JWT Editor Keys</strong> tab.' => 'Siapkan pasangan kunci RSA baru (misalnya pada tab <strong>JWT Editor Keys</strong>).',
    '[[A0]]Generate a new RSA key.[[/A0]]' => '[[A0]]Buat kunci RSA baru.[[/A0]]',
    'Send a request containing a JWT to Burp Repeater.' => 'Ambil permintaan HTTP yang membawa JWT aktif.',
    'In the message editor, switch to the extension-generated <strong>JSON Web Token</strong> tab and [[A0]]modify[[/A0]] the token\'s payload however you like.' => '[[A0]]Ubah isi klaim payload[[/A0]] JWT sesuai target.',
    'Click <strong>Attack</strong>, then select <strong>Embedded JWK</strong>. When prompted, select your newly generated RSA key.' => 'Pilih serangan <strong>Embedded JWK</strong> dan tandatangani dengan kunci RSA yang baru dibuat.',
    'Send the request to test how the server responds.' => 'Kirim ulang permintaan ke server dan amati responsnya.',
    'You can also perform this attack manually by adding the [[C0]] header yourself. However, you may also need to update the JWT\'s [[C1]] header parameter to match the [[C2]] of the embedded key. The extension\'s built-in attack takes care of this step for you.' => 'Bila menyunting manual, pastikan nilai [[C1]] di header sama dengan [[C2]] kunci yang disematkan pada [[C0]].',
    'Injecting self-signed JWTs via the jku parameter' => 'Menyuntikkan JWT bertanda tangan sendiri melalui parameter jku',
    'Instead of embedding public keys directly using the [[C0]] header parameter, some servers let you use the [[C1]] (JWK Set URL) header parameter to reference a JWK Set containing the key. When verifying the signature, the server fetches the relevant key from this URL.' => 'Alih-alih menyematkan kunci lewat [[C0]], sebagian server mengizinkan parameter [[C1]] untuk mengambil daftar kunci publik dari URL eksternal.',
    'JWK Set' => 'JWK Set',
    'A JWK Set is a JSON object containing an array of JWKs representing different keys. You can see an example of this below.' => 'JWK Set adalah objek JSON berisi array beberapa kunci JWK:',
    'JWK Sets like this are sometimes exposed publicly via a standard endpoint, such as [[C0]].' => 'JWK Set ini kerap dipublikasikan di endpoint standar seperti [[C0]].',
    'More secure websites will only fetch keys from trusted domains, but you can sometimes take advantage of URL parsing discrepancies to bypass this kind of filtering. We covered some [[A0]]examples of these[[/A0]] in our topic on SSRF.' => 'Jika server hanya mengambil dari domain tepercaya, Anda sering dapat melewati filter domainnya memakai [[A0]]inkonsistensi parsing URL / bypass SSRF[[/A0]] atau open redirect.',
    'Injecting self-signed JWTs via the kid parameter' => 'Menyuntikkan JWT bertanda tangan sendiri melalui parameter kid',
    'Servers may use several cryptographic keys for signing different kinds of data, not just JWTs. For this reason, the header of a JWT may contain a [[C0]] (Key ID) parameter, which helps the server identify which key to use when verifying the signature.' => 'Parameter [[C0]] membantu server memilih kunci verifikasi dari penyimpanan kunci.',
    "Verification keys are often stored as a JWK Set. In this case, the server may simply look for the JWK with the same [[C0]] as the token. However, the JWS specification doesn't define a concrete structure for this ID - it's just an arbitrary string of the developer's choosing. For example, they might use the [[C1]] parameter to point to a particular entry in a database, or even the name of a file." => 'Karena format [[C0]] tidak dibakukan, pengembang kadang menggunakannya sebagai nama file di sistem berkas atau kunci query di database ([[C1]]).',
    'If this parameter is also vulnerable to directory traversal, an attacker could potentially force the server to use an arbitrary file from its filesystem as the verification key.' => 'Jika parameter tersebut rentan terhadap directory traversal, penyerang dapat memaksa server membaca berkas sembarang dari sistem berkasnya sebagai kunci verifikasi:',
    'This is especially dangerous if the server also supports JWTs signed using a [[A0]]symmetric algorithm[[/A0]]. In this case, an attacker could potentially point the [[C0]] parameter to a predictable, static file, then sign the JWT using a secret that matches the contents of this file.' => 'Jika digabung dengan [[A0]]algoritma simetris[[/A0]], penyerang tinggal mengarahkan [[C0]] ke file yang isinya diketahui lalu menandatangani JWT dengan isi file tersebut.',
    'You could theoretically do this with any file, but one of the simplest methods is to use [[C0]], which is present on most Linux systems. As this is an empty file, reading it returns an empty string. Therefore, signing the token with a empty string will result in a valid signature.' => 'Target termudah di Linux adalah [[C0]] yang selalu mengembalikan string kosong, sehingga JWT cukup ditandatangani memakai secret string kosong.',
    'If the server stores its verification keys in a database, the [[C0]] header parameter is also a potential vector for SQL injection attacks.' => 'Jika kunci verifikasi disimpan di basis data, parameter [[C0]] juga berpotensi rentan terhadap SQL injection.',
    'Other interesting JWT header parameters' => 'Parameter header JWT menarik lainnya',
    'The following header parameters may also be interesting for attackers:' => 'Beberapa parameter header lain yang layak diperiksa saat audit JWT:',
    '[[C0]] (Content Type) - Sometimes used to declare a media type for the content in the JWT payload. This is usually omitted from the header, but the underlying parsing library may support it anyway. If you have found a way to bypass signature verification, you can try injecting a [[C1]] header to change the content type to [[C2]] or [[C3]], which can potentially enable new vectors for [[A0]]XXE[[/A0]] and [[A1]]deserialization[[/A1]] attacks.' => '[[C0]] (Content Type): dapat mengaktifkan parser [[C2]] atau [[C3]] di pustaka penerima sehingga membuka peluang [[A0]]XXE[[/A0]] atau [[A1]]deserialisasi tidak aman[[/A1]] pada [[C1]].',
    '[[C0]] (X.509 Certificate Chain) - Sometimes used to pass the X.509 public key certificate or certificate chain of the key used to digitally sign the JWT. This header parameter can be used to inject self-signed certificates, similar to the [[A0]][[C1]] header injection[[/A0]] attacks discussed above. Due to the complexity of the X.509 format and its extensions, parsing these certificates can also introduce vulnerabilities. Details of these attacks are beyond the scope of these materials, but for more details, check out [[A1]]CVE-2017-2800[[/A1]] and [[A2]]CVE-2018-2633[[/A2]].' => '[[C0]] (X.509 Certificate Chain): serupa injeksi [[A0]][[C1]][[/A0]], memungkinkan penyematan sertifikat X.509 palsu maupun kerentanan parser seperti [[A1]]CVE-2017-2800[[/A1]] dan [[A2]]CVE-2018-2633[[/A2]].',
    'JWT algorithm confusion' => 'Algorithm confusion pada JWT',
    'Even if a server uses robust secrets that you are unable to brute-force, you may still be able to forge valid JWTs by signing the token using an algorithm that the developers haven\'t anticipated. This is known as an algorithm confusion attack.' => 'Sekalipun rahasia server sangat kuat, pemalsuan token tetap mungkin jika server dapat dipaksa memverifikasi token memakai algoritma lain (algorithm confusion).',
    'JWT algorithm confusion attacks' => 'Serangan algorithm confusion JWT',
    'How to prevent JWT attacks' => 'Cara mencegah serangan JWT',
    'You can protect your own websites against many of the attacks we\'ve covered by taking the following high-level measures:' => 'Langkah inti mencegah berbagai serangan JWT di atas:',
    'Use an up-to-date library for handling JWTs and make sure your developers fully understand how it works, along with any security implications. Modern libraries make it more difficult for you to inadvertently implement them insecurely, but this isn\'t foolproof due to the inherent flexibility of the related specifications.' => 'Gunakan pustaka JWT versi terbaru dan pahami betul perilaku serta opsi algoritma yang diterimanya.',
    'Make sure that you perform robust signature verification on any JWTs that you receive, and account for edge-cases such as JWTs signed using unexpected algorithms.' => 'Selalu panggil verifikasi tanda tangan dan kunci algoritma yang diharapkan secara eksplisit pada konfigurasi server (tolak alg:none dan konversi simetris tak terduga).',
    'Enforce a strict whitelist of permitted hosts for the [[C0]] header.' => 'Terapkan whitelist domain tepercaya secara ketat jika mendukung parameter [[C0]].',
    'Make sure that you\'re not vulnerable to path traversal or SQL injection via the [[C0]] header parameter.' => 'Validasi parameter [[C0]] agar bebas dari path traversal maupun SQL injection.',
    'Additional best practice for JWT handling' => 'Praktik terbaik tambahan untuk penanganan JWT',
    'Although not strictly necessary to avoid introducing vulnerabilities, we recommend adhering to the following best practice when using JWTs in your applications:' => 'Tambahan praktik baik keamanan JWT:',
    'Always set an expiration date for any tokens that you issue.' => 'Selalu tetapkan waktu kedaluwarsa (klaim exp) pada setiap token.',
    'Avoid sending tokens in URL parameters where possible.' => 'Hindari mengirim JWT di dalam parameter URL.',
    'Include the [[C0]] (audience) claim (or similar) to specify the intended recipient of the token. This prevents it from being used on different websites.' => 'Sertakan dan validasi klaim [[C0]] agar token hanya berlaku untuk layanan tujuan.',
    'Enable the issuing server to revoke tokens (on logout, for example).' => 'Sediakan mekanisme pencabutan token saat pengguna keluar atau mengganti sandi.',

    // algorithm-confusion
    'Algorithm confusion attacks' => 'Serangan algorithm confusion',
    'Algorithm confusion attacks (also known as key confusion attacks) occur when an attacker is able to force the server to verify the signature of a JSON web token ([[A0]]JWT[[/A0]]) using a different algorithm than is intended by the website\'s developers. If this case isn\'t handled properly, this may enable attackers to forge valid JWTs containing arbitrary values without needing to know the server\'s secret signing key.' => 'Serangan algorithm confusion terjadi saat penyerang memaksa server memverifikasi [[A0]]JWT[[/A0]] dengan algoritma berbeda dari yang dirancang pengembang, sehingga tanda tangan palsu dapat diterima tanpa kunci privat server.',
    'Symmetric vs asymmetric algorithms' => 'Algoritma simetris vs asimetris',
    'JWTs can be signed using a range of different algorithms. Some of these, such as HS256 (HMAC + SHA-256) use a "symmetric" key. This means that the server uses a single key to both sign and verify the token. Clearly, this needs to be kept secret, just like a password.' => 'Algoritma simetris seperti HS256 memakai satu kunci rahasia yang sama untuk membuat dan memverifikasi tanda tangan.',
    'Other algorithms, such as RS256 (RSA + SHA-256) use an "asymmetric" key pair. This consists of a private key, which the server uses to sign the token, and a mathematically related public key that can be used to verify the signature.' => 'Algoritma asimetris seperti RS256 memakai pasangan kunci: kunci privat untuk menandatangani dan kunci publik untuk memverifikasi.',
    'As the names suggest, the private key must be kept secret, but the public key is often shared so that anybody can verify the signature of tokens issued by the server.' => 'Kunci privat wajib dirahasiakan, sedangkan kunci publik kerap dibagikan secara terbuka.',
    'How algorithm confusion vulnerabilities arise' => 'Bagaimana kerentanan algorithm confusion muncul',
    "Algorithm confusion vulnerabilities typically arise due to flawed implementation of JWT libraries. Although the actual verification process differs depending on the algorithm used, many libraries provide a single, algorithm-agnostic method for verifying signatures. These methods rely on the [[C0]] parameter in the token's header to determine the type of verification they should perform." => 'Banyak pustaka menyediakan fungsi verifikasi umum yang langsung membaca parameter header [[C0]] dari token untuk memilih algoritma.',
    'The following pseudo-code shows a simplified example of what the declaration for this generic [[C0]] method might look like in a JWT library:' => 'Contoh pseudokode metode [[C0]] yang bergantung pada header alg token:',
    'Problems arise when website developers who subsequently use this method assume that it will exclusively handle JWTs signed using an asymmetric algorithm like RS256. Due to this flawed assumption, they may always pass a fixed public key to the method as follows:' => 'Masalah muncul bila pengembang mengira hanya token RS256 yang masuk lalu meneruskan kunci publik tetap ke fungsi tersebut:',
    'In this case, if the server receives a token signed using a symmetric algorithm like HS256, the library\'s generic [[C0]] method will treat the public key as an HMAC secret. This means that an attacker could sign the token using HS256 and the public key, and the server will use the same public key to verify the signature.' => 'Jika penyerang mengganti alg menjadi HS256, metode [[C0]] menganggap kunci publik tersebut sebagai secret HMAC simetris sehingga tanda tangan buatan penyerang lolos verifikasi.',
    'The public key you use to sign the token must be absolutely identical to the public key stored on the server. This includes using the same format (such as X.509 PEM) and preserving any non-printing characters like newlines. In practice, you may need to experiment with different formatting in order for this attack to work.' => 'Format byte kunci publik (seperti X.509 PEM atau PKCS1 beserta karakter baris baru di akhir) harus identik persis dengan salinan yang dipegang server.',
    'Performing an algorithm confusion attack' => 'Melakukan serangan algorithm confusion',
    'An algorithm confusion attack generally involves the following high-level steps:' => 'Tahapan umum serangan algorithm confusion adalah:',
    '[[A0]]Obtain the server\'s public key[[/A0]]' => '[[A0]]Dapatkan kunci publik server[[/A0]]',
    '[[A0]]Convert the public key to a suitable format[[/A0]]' => '[[A0]]Konversi kunci publik ke format yang dipakai server[[/A0]]',
    '[[A0]]Create a malicious JWT[[/A0]] with a modified payload and the [[C0]] header set to [[C1]].' => '[[A0]]Modifikasi payload JWT[[/A0]] dengan header [[C0]] disetel ke [[C1]].',
    '[[A0]]Sign the token with HS256[[/A0]], using the public key as the secret.' => '[[A0]]Tandatangani token memakai HS256[[/A0]] menggunakan byte kunci publik sebagai secret.',
    'In this section, we\'ll walk through this process in more detail, demonstrating how you can perform this kind of attack using Burp Suite.' => 'Berikut rincian langkah-langkah eksekusinya.',
    'Step 1 - Obtain the server\'s public key' => 'Langkah 1 - Dapatkan kunci publik server',
    'Servers sometimes expose their public keys as JSON Web Key (JWK) objects via a standard endpoint mapped to [[C0]] or [[C1]], for example. These may be stored in an array of JWKs called [[C2]]. This is known as a JWK Set.' => 'Server kerap memublikasikan kunci publik dalam format JWK Set pada endpoint seperti [[C0]] atau [[C1]] di array [[C2]]:',
    'Even if the key isn\'t exposed publicly, you may be able to [[A0]]extract it from a pair of existing JWTs[[/A0]].' => 'Jika tidak dibuka secara publik, kunci publik RSA sering masih bisa [[A0]]diturunkan dari dua buah JWT sah[[/A0]].',
    'Step 2 - Convert the public key to a suitable format' => 'Langkah 2 - Konversi kunci publik ke format yang sesuai',
    'Although the server may expose their public key in JWK format, when verifying the signature of a token, it will use its own copy of the key from its local filesystem or database. This may be stored in a different format.' => 'Walaupun dipublikasikan sebagai JWK, server bisa jadi memverifikasi dengan salinan format PEM di berkas lokalnya.',
    'In order for the attack to work, the version of the key that you use to sign the JWT must be identical to the server\'s local copy. In addition to being in the same format, every single byte must match, including any non-printing characters.' => 'Setiap byte hasil konversi termasuk spasi atau baris baru wajib cocok dengan format kunci di server.',
    "For the purpose of this example, let's assume that we need the key in X.509 PEM format. You can convert a JWK to a PEM using the [[A0]]JWT Editor[[/A0]] extension in Burp as follows:" => 'Contoh konversi JWK menjadi secret X.509 PEM (dapat pula dilakukan memakai [[A0]]ekstensi JWT Editor[[/A0]]):',
    'With the extension loaded, in Burp\'s main tab bar, go to the <strong>JWT Editor Keys</strong> tab.' => 'Buka pengelola kunci kriptografi (seperti tab <strong>JWT Editor Keys</strong>).',
    'Click <strong>New RSA</strong> Key. In the dialog, paste the JWK that you obtained earlier.' => 'Muat kunci JWK publik server sebagai kunci RSA.',
    'Select the <strong>PEM</strong> radio button and copy the resulting PEM key.' => 'Ekspor atau konversi ke format <strong>PEM</strong> X.509 lalu salin teksnya.',
    'Go to the <strong>Decoder</strong> tab and Base64-encode the PEM.' => 'Encode teks PEM tersebut ke format Base64.',
    'Go back to the <strong>JWT Editor Keys</strong> tab and click <strong>New Symmetric Key</strong>.' => 'Buat kunci simetris baru untuk penandatanganan HMAC.',
    'In the dialog, click <strong>Generate</strong> to generate a new key in JWK format.' => 'Siapkan struktur kunci simetris JWK baru.',
    'Replace the generated value for the [[C0]] parameter with a Base64-encoded PEM key that you just copied.' => 'Ganti nilai kunci [[C0]] pada JWK simetris tersebut dengan PEM ber-encode Base64 tadi.',
    'Save the key.' => 'Simpan kunci simetris untuk langkah penandatanganan.',
    'Step 3 - Modify your JWT' => 'Langkah 3 - Modifikasi JWT Anda',
    'Once you have the public key in a suitable format, you can [[A0]]modify the JWT[[/A0]] however you like. Just make sure that the [[C0]] header is set to [[C1]].' => 'Ubah payload klaim sesuai target dan pastikan header [[C0]] diubah ke [[C1]].',
    'Step 4 - Sign the JWT using the public key' => 'Langkah 4 - Tandatangani JWT dengan kunci publik',
    '[[A0]]Sign the token[[/A0]] using the HS256 algorithm with the RSA public key as the secret.' => '[[A0]]Tandatangani token[[/A0]] dengan HS256 memakai kunci publik tersebut.',
    'Deriving public keys from existing tokens' => 'Menurunkan kunci publik dari token yang sudah ada',
    'In cases where the public key isn\'t readily available, you may still be able to test for algorithm confusion by deriving the key from a pair of existing JWTs. This process is relatively simple using tools such as [[C0]]. You can find this, along with several other useful scripts, on the [[A0]][[C1]] GitHub repository[[/A0]].' => 'Bila endpoint JWKS tidak tersedia, modulus RSA kunci publik dapat dihitung mundur dari dua token JWT bertanda tangan RS256 menggunakan [[C0]] di [[A0]]repositori [[C1]][[/A0]].',
    'We have also created a simplified version of this tool, which you can run as a single command:' => 'Tersedia pula utilitas kontainer ringkas untuk menghitung kandidat kuncinya:',
    'You need the Docker CLI to run either version of the tool. The first time you run this command, it will automatically pull the image from Docker Hub, which may take a few minutes.' => 'Pastikan Docker CLI tersedia di mesin Anda saat menjalankan perintah tersebut.',
    "This uses the JWTs that you provide to calculate one or more potential values of [[C0]]. Don't worry too much about what this means - all you need to know is that only one of these matches the value of [[C1]] used by the server's key. For each potential value, our script outputs:" => 'Skrip tersebut menghitung kandidat nilai modulus [[C0]] (dan [[C1]]) dari tanda tangan dua token lalu menghasilkan:',
    'A Base64-encoded PEM key in both X.509 and PKCS1 format.' => 'Kandidat kunci PEM ber-encode Base64 dalam format X.509 dan PKCS1.',
    'A forged JWT signed using each of these keys.' => 'Contoh JWT palsu yang sudah ditandatangani dengan tiap kandidat kunci.',
    'To identify the correct key, use Burp Repeater to send a request containing each of the forged JWTs. Only one of these will be accepted by the server. You can then use the matching key to construct an algorithm confusion attack.' => 'Uji tiap JWT kandidat ke server; hanya satu yang akan diterima, dan kunci itulah yang dapat dipakai untuk eksploitasi penuh.',
    'For more information on how this process works, and details of how to use the standard [[C0]] tool, please refer to the documentation provided in the [[A0]]repository[[/A0]].' => 'Lihat dokumentasi [[A0]]repositori[[/A0]] untuk rincian cara kerja [[C0]].',
    'For more labs, check out the rest of our topic on JWT attacks.' => 'Jelajahi lab lainnya pada topik serangan JWT.',
];
